# Test: `ze --plugin ze.fib-kernel config validate` refuses a config holding
#       `fib { dummy { } }` with the exact `--plugin` What / Why / Fix lines.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-fib-dummy AC-4, A-1 -- the process-wide `--plugin` record
#            reaches `ze config validate` through `candidatePluginSelection`,
#            refusing `fib dummy` when `fib-kernel` is selected on the command
#            line and naming `start ze without --plugin ze.fib-kernel`.
# PREVENTS:  `--plugin ze.fib-kernel` bypassing the no-plane refusal at
#            `ze config validate`.

stdin=dummy-only:terminator=EOF_CONF
fib {
	dummy { }
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze --plugin ze.fib-kernel config validate -:stdin=dummy-only
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=fib dummy is configured and the plugin fib-kernel is selected
expect=stdout:contains=fib dummy is the choice to program no route, and fib kernel programs the kernel data plane
expect=stdout:contains=fix: delete fib dummy, or start ze without --plugin ze.fib-kernel
